## Part I: Anatomy and Visualization of the ET Lattice

### 1.1 The Multiplicative Manifold and Its Log-Space Image

Every positive real number `r ∈ (0, +∞)` lives on the multiplicative manifold. Under the logarithm map:

```
log₂ : (ℝ⁺, ×) → (ℝ, +)

Multiplication → Addition
Powers         → Scaling
Ratios         → Differences
```

The entire infinite richness of (ℝ⁺, ×) is faithfully mapped to the real number line. The ET lattice operates on this additive image, placing grid points at every integer multiple of `1/12`:

```
Lattice ℒ = { k/12 : k ∈ ℤ }   ⊂ ℝ

Each grid point k/12 corresponds to the ratio 2^(k/12) in the original multiplicative space.
```

### 1.2 Visualization I: The Infinite Log-Line

Below is the primary visualization. The horizontal axis is log-space (additive). The vertical markers are the 12ET lattice points. The unison `r = 1` sits at the origin `k = 0`.

```
