## Part III: The Special Case of 0/1 — The Annihilating Boundary

### 3.1 Mathematical Status

The value `0 = 0/1` is the **infimum** of `(ℝ⁺, ×)`. It is not an element of the manifold — `ℝ⁺ = (0, +∞)` excludes zero by definition. Zero is the limit approached but never reached.

Under the logarithm map:

```
lim_{r → 0⁺} log₂(r) = −∞

The lattice coordinate:
k = round(12 × log₂(0/1)) = round(12 × (−∞)) = −∞

→ 0/1 projects to k = −∞.
   This is NOT a lattice point. It is the BOUNDARY of the lattice.
```

There is no sublattice family for `0/1`. The concept of `d = 12/gcd(|−∞|, 12)` is undefined. The framework `(ℝ⁺, ×)` breaks at `r = 0`.

### 3.2 The Boundary as Physical Vacuum

The limit `r → 0` corresponds to ratios vanishing to nothing — complete annihilation of a multiplicative relationship. In physics:

```
r → 0  means:  one quantity becomes infinitely smaller than the reference
            OR: a coupling vanishes entirely (decoupling limit)
            OR: an amplitude is exponentially suppressed to nothing

log-space: k → −∞  (the ratio escapes all finite lattice representation)
```

This is the **"multiplicative vacuum"** — the state where no ratio is left to describe. It is the absence of D-binding: the pure Point `P` with no Descriptor constraint active.

### 3.3 How 0/1 Falls on the Lattice

```
0/1 DOES NOT FALL ON THE LATTICE.
It is the asymptotic limit of the negative lattice half-line.

Visualization of the approach:

r = 1/2      → k = −12  (one octave below origin)
r = 1/4      → k = −24  (two octaves below)
r = 1/8      → k = −36  (three octaves below)
r = 1/1024   → k = −120 (ten octaves below)
r = 10⁻¹⁰   → k ≈ −399 (experimental θ̄ bound)
r = (1/12)^10 → k ≈ −430 (ET cascade bound for θ̄)
r → 0        → k → −∞   (the boundary, never reached)
```

Every finite `k` corresponds to a non-zero ratio. The lattice is infinite — it has no last point before the boundary. Zero is the limit of the lattice, not a point within it. The lattice "reaches toward" zero without ever arriving.

### 3.4 Physical Interpretation

`0/1 = 0` as a lattice position is the **complete absence of all Descriptor binding**. Nothing is described; no ratio exists. This is the pure `P` state — infinite, unbound, prior to all constraint. The approach `r → 0` is the progressive unbinding of Descriptors, one cascade level at a time, each step moving the lattice coordinate by one more semitone below.

